  "semantic_slots": {
    "objects": "Actual gamma_n=Measure.pi (fun _:Fin n=>gaussianReal 0 1), real f and D_i(x)=fderiv R f x(Pi.single i 1). Phi(t)=t log t, homogeneous entropy integral Phi(f²)-Phi(integral f²).",
    "domains": "All natural n including0; canonical finite Pi real Borel topology with default sup norm, coordinate-square energy explicitly. C2 compact signed f. True probability and actual L1 f²/Phi(f²)/each D_i²/full finite sum are produced, not supplied.",
    "quantifiers": "forall n forall f, C2 f and HasCompactSupport f imply domains and scalar LSI. Scalar/head and tail original slices for every fixed complementary coordinate are internal. No selected positive density or prechosen LSI witness.",
    "assumptions": "Only n,f,C2,compact support at sealed compact interface. Source background external W12/differentiable/continuous-partials/Phi-L1 contract is broader; compactness is an explicit authored sufficient class, not a paper standing hypothesis. No mass-one f², positivity, bound, RMS regularity, domain, inequality or measure-law certificate may become a new public binder.",
    "conclusion": "Genuine homogeneous Ent_gamma_n(f²)<=2 integral sum_i D_i² together with actual four L1 clauses. This finite-product compact background is not the printed Wasserstein inequality and does not include noncompact or Hilbert transport.",
    "scopes": "SPHMCv1 FIRST4.6 invokes Gaussian LSI and T2 without printing tensorization. Pinned SLT supplies external unbounded W12 finite-coordinate entropy plus energy proof; authored original-slice binary39/scalar38 dimension induction is a distinct sufficient compact OR route. No Gaussian T2/FIRST4.6/fullpaper or implementation credit.",
    "constant_dependencies": "Variance exactly1 in each coordinate; function-LSI coefficient2 dimension-free. n0 singleton Dirac makes entropy0 and empty energy0; n1 scalarvariance1. Future f=sqrtq has energy I/4, giving KL<=I/2 only after real Hilbert/noncompact/coherence adapters, and W2²<=2KL is separate."
  },
